"Done — the `fmtcsv` project is in place and all 12 tests pass.\n\n**Files created**\n\n- `fmtcsv.py` — CLI implementation. Parses with Python's `csv` module defaults, so quoted fields with commas work and exact field content (including leading/trailing spaces inside quotes) is preserved. The first line is the header; it prints `Total rows`, `Total columns`, and `First data row`. Missing files exit with code 2 via argparse.\n- `test_fmtcsv.py` — 12 pytest tests covering: simple CSVs, quoted fields with commas, spaces inside quotes, escaped quotes (`\"\"`), multiline quoted fields counted as one row, header-only and empty files, output formatting, error handling, and a real subprocess end-to-end run.\n- `README.md` — usage and test instructions.\n\n**Test results**\n\n```\n12 passed in 0.04s\n```\n\n**Demo run** on a file with quoted spaces/commas:\n\n```\nTotal rows: 2\nTotal columns: 3\nFirst data row: ['Alice', '30', '  likes pie, and cake  ']\n```\n\nNote: the default `/opt/venv` Python had no pytest and no permission to install, so I created `.venv/` in the workspace with pytest installed. Run tests with:\n\n```\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest test_fmtcsv.py -v\n```"